Changes made to the original
----------------------------

This is an adaptation, and ShareAlike applies to it. What was changed:

  * A 300-row subset of the development split was selected (seed 42), not the whole set.
  * Rows whose gold query returns an empty result set were removed.
  * Each row was labelled with a difficulty band, computed with Spider's own official
    hardness classifier, and assigned to a tuning or holdout split.
  * Rows were reshaped into one flat JSON object per line.
  * Only the 18 SQLite databases these 300 questions need are included.

build_slice.py in this directory reproduces all of it.

What ShareAlike means here
--------------------------

Anything derived from this data must also be shared under CC BY-SA 4.0 with the attribution
above. That obligation travels with the data, not with the code, and it does not go away if
the data is copied somewhere else. Publishing this repository, or a generated demo project
containing these rows, is a redistribution: this file must travel with it.
